<$fill $name="body">

!! Q: I changed a date and the count did not change.

The counts are a snapshot. Click ↻ or reload. This is on purpose: nothing runs while you edit.

!! Q: An item I expected is missing.

It may sit in an earlier area (first match wins), be muted (see the footer of the panel), or have a blank or non-date value in the area's date field (`wf-days` drops those).

!! Q: The dock shows `!`.

The area filter is broken. Hover the `!` to see the error. The other areas still work.

!! Q: I drag a row and no ring opens.

No action matched this item. An action needs `wf.group`, and its `wf.filter` must return something for the item. Without a filter it always matches.

!! Q: An action has no tile for a value like `+1d`.

Values with `+` or `-` must be bracketed in `wf.tiles`: `[[today]] [[+1d]]`.

!! Q: The action failed halfway; is it undone?

No. Actions are not transactional. A failing action shows a notice and leaves no mark, but what it changed before the failure stays.

!! Q: I defined a group or action twice.

With the same `wf.name` (group or recipe) the first one found wins. To override a shipped one, use the same //title// as the shadow; your tiddler then replaces it.

!! Q: Move does the wrong default.

A group's default tile is the group's `wf.default` action. When it has several tiles, `wf.default-value` picks one. Move uses the day strip's `+1d`.

!! Q: Does clicking an item close the panel?

No, so you can triage several. A click outside closes it, and that click still reaches what is underneath.

!! Q: I installed it and nothing changed.

JS modules need a server restart (`click-outside.js`, `ring-layer.js`, `date-operators.js`, …).

!! Q: The dock is hidden behind the sidebar button.

At `top-right` it can sit under the Vanilla sidebar toggle. Use another corner or move the dock.

!! Q: Tiles are cut off on a small window.

With 5 or 6 groups, a viewport of about 440 px height or less can clamp tiles. Use a taller window.

</$fill>
</$transclude>
